Subject: [PATCH] qdsp6v2: complete PCM copies and preserve per-stream buffer ownership

The downstream PCM .copy callbacks truncate an ALSA request to one DSP
buffer and return success, discarding playback data or unread capture data.
Keep partial buffers per stream and transfer every requested byte across
buffer boundaries. Return errors for signals, timeouts and failed transfers.

Accumulate small playback writes before RUN, record each submitted length,
and send queued writes from process context. Serialize STOP/EOS behind any
write already selected, cancel work before freeing the client, and keep
capture metadata and wait queues local to the stream. Propagate prepare
errors and constrain period counts to those supported by the Q6 ring mask.

Source: msfkonsole/android_kernel_xiaomi_dior
Base: 12f40d54ab4e34dabaeb8dd7979bedc3cc8fa064
This does not change mixer routes, gain, firmware, DTB or ramdisk.

